}
```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
-  public void reload() {
-    for (ServerCommand serverCommand : serverCommands.values()) {
-      ((AbstractCommand) serverCommand).reloadText();
```
Reason:
The removal of the `reload()` method, which iterated through all server and player commands to call `reloadText()`, meant that any updates to command definitions or help text were not applied, resulting in outdated help information when the `/help` command was invoked.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
public void reload() {
    for (ServerCommand serverCommand : serverCommands.values()) {
        ((AbstractCommand) serverCommand).reloadText();
    }
    for (PlayerCommand playerCommand : playerCommands.values()) {
        ((AbstractCommand) playerCommand).reloadText();
    }
}
```
Reason:
Reintroducing the `reload()` method restores the functionality to update the help text for all commands, ensuring that any changes made to command definitions or help text are reflected correctly when the `/help` command is executed.

